  - m_Id: 3157871247360
    m_Localized: Fiber coupler
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3197780049920
    m_Localized: Camera
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3253925003264
    m_Localized: "45\xB0 Mirror"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3273197830144
    m_Localized: "90\xB0 Mirror"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3294198710272
    m_Localized: Beam splitter
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3326599708672
    m_Localized: Waveplate
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3350880534528
    m_Localized: Double slit
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3386104299520
    m_Localized: Tunnel effect
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3413501493248
    m_Localized: Polarizer
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3439925608448
    m_Localized: Glass wedge
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 37150951948288
    m_Localized: 'Create a periscope in the top left corner of the board.


      A
      periscope shifts the beam path parallel and is therefore used to reflect the
      laser from the quantum case onto the playing field.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 37833151299584
    m_Localized: 'Create a periscope in the top right corner of the board.


      This
      periscope guides the beam path back into the quantum case in parallel to feed
      it to the detector.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 38101519646720
    m_Localized: "Create a new QuBrick and change the type to 45\xB0 mirror. Place
      the QuBrick at the marked location.\n\nTap the QuBrick's icon on its top to
      open the settings menu. Select \"Change Type\" and set the QuBrick to \"45\xB0
      Mirror.\" Then, close the menu.\n\nPlace the QuBrick at the marked location
      to redirect the beam downwards."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 38356667547648
    m_Localized: "Place a new QuBrick at the marked location and change the type
      to beamsplitter. \n\nThe beam splitter uses a semi-transparent mirror to reflect
      some of the light at 90\xB0 and allow the remaining light to pass through the
      mirror. This component is integral to the construction of a Michelson interferrometer."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 38557893476352
    m_Localized: "Place two new QuBricks at the marked location and change the type
      to 90\xB0 mirror.\n\nThe 90\xB0 mirrors form the arms of the Michelson interferometer
      and reflect the beams directly back to the beam splitter.\nShifting these mirrors
      results in different interference patterns on the detector."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 38690097938432
    m_Localized: "Place two more QuBricks with the 45\xB0 mirror type.\n\nRotate
      the mirrors so that you direct the beam back into the right periscope."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 38806838001664
    m_Localized: 'Perfect, you have successfully completed the experimental setup.


      In
      a real experiment, the interference pattern of the two superimposed light beams
      would now be displayed.

      We are currently working on the visualization.
      Hopefully they enjoyed their trip to the learning environment.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 51424176848896
    m_Localized: en
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 344409720438784
    m_Localized: Show Interference-pattern
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 344498601934848
    m_Localized: Change Instruction
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 344535763468288
    m_Localized: Show Instruction
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 393580062130176
    m_Localized: "The periscope directs the laser from the light source onto\nthe
      surface. It can also be used to \nto reflect the laser back into the case \nand
      feed it to the detector unit.\nOn the left they are connected to the source.
      \nOn the right, they are connected to the detector."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 393856265437184
    m_Localized: "Lossless polarization manipulation\r\n\u03BB/2 or \u03BB/4 integrated
      plates\r\nFor advanced polarization experiments such as quantum cryptography
      & tomography\r"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 394081147240448
    m_Localized: "Reflects the incoming beam in the direction \ndirection from which
      the beam came. The mirror \ndistance can be adjustable in the wavelength range
      \nof the light, so that the the path travelled by the laser \nbeam can be manipulated."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 394236940468224
    m_Localized: "The mirror positioned at a 45\xB0 angle reflects the beam \nbeam
      by 90\xB0."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 394411461263360
    m_Localized: "\rCouples the beam into optical fibers\r\nEfficient, automatic
      fiber coupling possible\r\nEnables the connection of further detectors and
      the combination with external setups\r"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 394557787947008
    m_Localized: "A classic for interference phenomena\r\nDifferent slit widths,
      grids, individual slits\r\nSpecial token for double-slit experiments with single
      photons or bright light\r"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 394748213542912
    m_Localized: "\rMeasurement of the laser beam\r\nView via display & external
      devices\r\nBeam adjustment, interference phenomena with bright light\r"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 394883165274112
    m_Localized: "A semi-transparent mirror positioned at a 45\xB0 angle. \nHalf
      of the incoming beam is transmitted straight ahead and the other half is deflected
      at a 90\xB0 angle. \nOften used for interferometry or quantum erasers. "
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 395085402030080
    m_Localized: 'Distance-dependent prism transmission

      Controlled via Quantenkoffer
      & external devices

      Special token for the tunnel effect based on the

      frustrated
      total internal reflection'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 395782830899200
    m_Localized: "The polarization of an electro-\r\nmagnetic  wave  refers  to 
      the  di-\r\nrection of oscillation of its electric \r\nfield. This token is
      a type of filter \r\nthat transmits only the light of a \r\ncertain polarization."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 396403822772224
    m_Localized: "Changes the optical path length\r\nOffset adjustable with \u03BCm
      accuracy\r\nSpecial token for interference experiments,\r\nHong-Ou-Mandel effect"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 397216162988032
    m_Localized: Polarizer
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 397488436232192
    m_Localized: Glass Wedge
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 397719022288896
    m_Localized: Tunnel effect
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 397908470611968
    m_Localized: Beam Splitter
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 398119293108224
    m_Localized: Camera
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 398505773056000
    m_Localized: Double slit
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 398694114082816
    m_Localized: Fiber Coupler
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 398906815627264
    m_Localized: "Mirror 45\xB0"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 399130992787456
    m_Localized: "Mirror 90\xB0"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 399288329519104
    m_Localized: Periscope
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 399433687318528
    m_Localized: Waveplate
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 417130592550912
    m_Localized: David
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 721971575472128
    m_Localized: 'Hello, this is an introduction to the operation of the virtual
      quantum suitcase.

      Tap Next below this text to begin the tutorial.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 722567162445824
    m_Localized: 'Press the marked button on the left edge of the quantum suitcase
      to create a periscope at that location.

      A periscope on the left side
      of the case is used to reflect the laser from the quantum case onto the playing
      field.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 723949101727744
    m_Localized: 'Press the marked button on the right edge of the quantum suitcase
      to create a periscope at this point.

      A periscope on the right side of
      the case is used to reflect the laser back from the playing field to the quantum
      case.

      Now the path of the laser from the input to the output is displayed
      visually.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 724842039689216
    m_Localized: Introduction
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 726109847764992
    m_Localized: "Create a new QuBrick by pressing the + sign in the middle right
      of the quantum suitcase.\nBy default, a newly created QuBrick is of the \u201C45\xB0
      mirror\u201D type."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 751528865120256
    m_Localized: Back
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 751580647997440
    m_Localized: Next
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 757002029187072
    m_Localized: 'Place the newly created QUBrick on the marked field by picking
      it up with your fingers and dragging it across the field until you hold it
      over the marked field.

      Now drop the QUBrick on the marked space.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 759765064695808
    m_Localized: "Create a new QuBrick and place it on the marked space.\nThe QuBrick
      can be rotated via the QuBrick menu.\nTo access the menu, tap the icon at the
      top of the brick you just placed.\nTap the \"Rotate left\" or \"Rotate right\"
      button in the bottom menu bar twice to rotate the token by 180\xB0."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 768607148261376
    m_Localized: "Create a new QuBrick and place it on the marked space.\nThe QuBrick
      type can be changed via the QuBrick menu.\nCall up the menu of the placed block
      and switch to the \u201CChange Type\u201D category. Change the QuBrick's type
      to \"Beam Splitter\"."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 770083404857344
    m_Localized: 'Congratulations, you now know how to use the virtual quantum suitcase.


      The
      incoming laser can now be displayed using the "Show interference pattern" switch
      on the right side of the lid.


      If several lasers overlap there, the
      interference pattern will also be displayed there.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2535753553494016
    m_Localized: Introduction
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2535958873063424
    m_Localized: Michelson-Interferometer
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10910647907467264
    m_Localized: Lightspeed experiment
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10914024884224000
    m_Localized: Lightspeed-experiment
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10915314049695744
    m_Localized: 'Create a Beamsplitter at the marked position.


      The Beam
      Splitter lets part of the light through but reflects another part onto the
      gameboard'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10915726567882752
    m_Localized: 'Create a Beamsplitter at the marked position.


      The second
      Beam Splitter also lets part of the light from the first Beamsplitter through
      but also takes in light from the gameboard below it and also reflects it to
      the periscope on its right'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10916031611224064
    m_Localized: "Create a 45\xB0 mirror at the marked position.\n\nThe Mirror reflects
      the Light coming from the first Beam splitter to the right side of the gameboard"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10916595493453824
    m_Localized: "Create a 45\xB0 mirror at the marked position.\n\nThe mirror reflects
      the light coming from the first mirror back to the second beamsplitter"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10916738875736064
    m_Localized: You can now measure the speed of light, since you know the offset
      of the Interference in addition to the extra distance the second beam has to
      take along the Mirrors in comparison to the unhindered Beam on the bottom of
      the gameboard
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10919139057811456
    m_Localized: "Perfect, you have successfully completed the test setup. \nYou
      can now fire a laser beam under the periscope on the left-hand side. \nOn the
      right behind the beam splitter you will see the interfered waves. \nYou can
      then try to influence the path using the options of the 90\xB0 mirror and trigger
      a new light wave. "
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10919224722276352
    m_Localized: 'Create a periscope in the bottom right corner of the board.


      This
      periscope guides the beam path back into the quantum case in parallel to feed
      it to the detector.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 13064302903377920
    m_Localized: Build automatically
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 13088954237272064
    m_Localized: Clear
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 21089938293080064
    m_Localized: Interference
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30065524533313536
    m_Localized: "Create a new building block and change it to \"Mirror 45\xB0\"\r\nPlace
      this so that the beam reflected upwards by the beam splitter is reflected into
      the periscope on the upper right side of the playing field.\r\n\r\nThis directs
      the beam back into the periscope so that it can be measured."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
