  - m_Id: 64536832232607744
    m_Localized: GhostImaging Experiment
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 65547612496146432
    m_Localized: Array detector
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 65547765789569024
    m_Localized: An array detector consists of an array of sensors or pixels that
      measure the intensity of light or other radiation reflected or transmitted
      by the object.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 65548760351322112
    m_Localized: Bucket detector
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 65548836503105536
    m_Localized: 'A bucket detector is a single sensor that measures the intensity
      of incoming light.













'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 66298294739357696
    m_Localized: Resulting Image
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 66298379942449152
    m_Localized: Reading the array detector exactly when a photon hits the bucket
      detector results in an shadow image of the object in front of the bucket detector.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 66987216793317376
    m_Localized: Laser pump
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 66987467121963008
    m_Localized: These pumps supply the energy needed to stimulate a laser medium
      and generate the emission of laser light. They often consist of high-power
      lamps, laser diodes, or other light sources that provide the necessary energy
      to initiate laser activity.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 66987652657000448
    m_Localized: Spontaneous Parametric Down-Conversion
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 66987853769682944
    m_Localized: A photon splits into two photons of lower energy levels when propagating
      through a nonlinear crystal material.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 67050784129626112
    m_Localized: Clear Result
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 67051135230619648
    m_Localized: Raster laser
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 67051233779986432
    m_Localized: Start laser
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 67067834327707648
    m_Localized: Change Shape
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 101122084965511168
    m_Localized: Error
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 101122186312478720
    m_Localized: wrong Placement
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 101122296320684032
    m_Localized: wrong rotation
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 101122413010415616
    m_Localized: wrong type
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 101515024518934528
    m_Localized: Virtual Quantumcase
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 112634469444562944
    m_Localized: "Please create a new QuBrick of type 90\xB0 mirror and place it
      at this position."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 112634953307860992
    m_Localized: "Now open the settings dialogue by tapping on the block. Select
      the options at the bottom left to vary the distance of the 90\xB0 mirror. This
      allows you to vary the distance of the laser to this mirror in the order of
      magnitude of the wavelength (lambda)."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 112652329386586112
    m_Localized: "You are now guided through the Michelson interferrometer setup.
      \nIt is used to measure particularly small differences in distance.\nIt utilises
      the effect of the inteference of light for this purpose. "
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 112653070868230144
    m_Localized: "When two light waves meet, they overlap. \nAs a result, the waves
      influence each other and their wave character changes. \nThis superposition
      depends on the distance that the waves have travelled relative to each other.\nFor
      example, if the distance is the same, the wave is amplified because the crests
      of the first light wave meet the crests of the second light wave exactly. "
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 112656296497721344
    m_Localized: "Now you can press the \u2018Start laser\u2019 button on the left-hand
      side of the case. \nIf everything has worked, you will see a red beam following
      your setup across the track field."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 141647714762313728
    m_Localized: Settings
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 141647896530866176
    m_Localized: Close settings
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 141648197899997184
    m_Localized: ' Up/Down'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 141648300962435072
    m_Localized: Left/Right
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 141648380092174336
    m_Localized: Forward/Back
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 141648671055237120
    m_Localized: AR Position settings
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 159799728175841280
    m_Localized: "Place a new QuBrick and set its type to a 45\xB0 mirror.\r\n\r\nTurn
      the lever until the 45\xB0 mirror symbol appears on the display. If the symbol
      on the QuBrick does not change, press the lever button once."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 159804122359398400
    m_Localized: "Press the lever on the side until the arrows on the display no
      longer highlight the mirror symbol but the number below it. This number indicates
      the phase shift of the waves. \n\nIf the numbers on both mirrors are the same,
      constructive interference occurs because their distances are identical. A difference
      of 0.5, for example, 0.5 on one and 0 on the other, results in destructive
      interference, as one mirror is shifted by half a wavelength.\r\n"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 159807282549358592
    m_Localized: "Perfect! You have successfully completed the experimental setup.\r\n\r\nYou
      can now fire a laser beam using the red button. To the right, behind the beam
      splitter, you will see the interfered waves. You can then try to adjust the
      path length of the 90\xB0 mirror and trigger a new light wave."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 160490863722496000
    m_Localized: 
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
